  "worked_solution": "Let $k(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x-4}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=k(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267656/assets/22d381f28b74d851369a40ef1c1f5bb6ef7fb22c11a7afb0145587480c0a7ccb.png)\n\nThe graph shows that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }k(x)=\\infty .\n$$",
